{
  "about": "Subagents (subagents.md, spec 3.3.0): which model a subagent runs on, and when subagents are offered. `models`: the models the person may use, by served id — `id` at its connection, display `name`, `capacity` (models/schema.json; {} — no limit); `session`: the session's model, one of them. `op` `model` — a task or team_add call with `model` (absent: none given) after the person typed `said` in this session (oldest first; `other`: texts that are not the person's — the model's, a tool's) — answers `{model}`: the served id the subagent runs on, or `{refused}`: the text, word for word (loop.json subagents.texts). `op` `offer` (`subagents`: enabled, default true) — `{offered, own, note}`: whether the Subagents setting and the team tools are offered, whether the session's model can serve its own subagents, and the note line that says it cannot (context.note.team_own) where subagents are offered, else null. LLeMbas: services/subagents.py; CLI: team/subagents.ts.",
